  Q2. Can we override static methods?

  No. Static methods belong to the class, not individual objects.

  If a child class declares a static method with the same signature, it is called method hiding, not overriding.

  Q3. Can we override private methods?

  No. Private methods are not visible to child classes, so they cannot be overridden.

  Q4. Can we override a method with a different return type?

  Only if the return type is compatible.

  For example, if the parent returns Number, the child can return Integer because Integer is a subclass of Number.

  Q5. Can constructors be overridden?

  No. Constructors are not inherited, so they cannot be overridden. However, constructors can be overloaded.

